    // attachments) ends, and streamInput() closes stdin behind it, so those
    // runs cannot be steered -- and must not be, or the message would vanish
    // into a closed pipe. Read at the query() call site, with no await between
    // here and the kitSteerable.add() below, so the flag cannot drift to
    // another run.
    kitPromptWasString = typeof prompt === 'string';
    return prompt;
