 * The CLI applies a mid-turn frame to the run in flight but records nothing, so
 * after a reload the message is simply gone -- CloudCLI reads its history from
 * that transcript and there is no second copy anywhere. Append it in the shape
 * the CLI writes for a user turn, chained onto the newest entry: the reader
 * takes it for a normal user message, and the CLI replays it on the next resume
 * rather than continuing a conversation it has no record of being redirected.
 * @param {string} sessionId - Session identifier
 * @param {string} text - What was said to the run
 * @param {string} timestamp - When it was said, ISO 8601, for history ordering
 * @returns {Promise<void>} Resolves once the line is on disk
